CONTEXT Permits INCLUDES Registry FROM "../contexts/registry.adl" AS Reg
CONTEXT Permits IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Permits
{+ The permit system of the example in the article on multi-context information systems.
It includes the population register under the alias Reg.
Both contexts have a relation `address` and a concept `Address`, which mean different things:
the home address of a person, and the site to which a permit applies.
The prefix keeps them apart. +}


RELATION applicant[Permit*Reg.Person] [UNI,TOT]
RELATION address[Permit*Address] [UNI]

POPULATION applicant[Permit*Reg.Person] CONTAINS
  [ ("permit1", "p1")
  ; ("permit2", "p2")
  ]
POPULATION address[Permit*Address] CONTAINS
  [ ("permit1", "Harbour Road 12")
  ]

-- A rule of this context over data of the included context.
-- Person p2 has no address in the register, so permit2 violates this rule.
-- A clerk has to restore it, which is why it is a business constraint.
RULE located : applicant |- applicant;Reg.address;Reg.address~
MEANING "Every applicant has an address in the register."
ROLE Clerk MAINTAINS located

ENDCONTEXT
